License:    MIT. Full text: LICENSE
Copyright:  Tatsuhiro Tsujikawa and the nghttp2 contributors
Modified:   yes, by tools/update-nghttp2 only; see "Patches" below

Design references: §48 (vendoring policy), §65 (HTTP/2), decisions D-89 and
D-96.

Update with tools/update-nghttp2. Do not edit these files by hand: the
patches below are applied by that script, which fails if upstream moves a
patch site, and a hand edit would be lost on the next update or, worse,
recorded by tools/vendor/record as if it were upstream.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
What is here
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every .c and .h of upstream's lib/, nghttp2/nghttp2.h from lib/includes/,
and nghttp2/nghttp2ver.h generated from its template. sfparse.{c,h} (MIT,
the RFC 9651 structured-field parser) ship inside upstream's lib/ and are
included. The applications in src/, the Python bindings, the build system
and config.h are not.

zuhttp's driver is src/zuh_h2.c. It moves bytes between a zuh_stream and the
session with nghttp2_session_mem_recv2() and nghttp2_session_mem_send2();
nghttp2 never sees a socket.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Patches (design §48)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. NDEBUG is defined (src/Makevars{,.win}.in), so the assert() calls
   compile out.
2. Each of the 13 abort() calls after assert(0) on an unreachable switch arm
   (10 in sfparse.c, 3 in nghttp2_session.c) returns an error instead:
   SFPARSE_ERR_PARSE, NGHTTP2_ERR_CALLBACK_FAILURE, 0 from the two uint32_t
   settings getters, and an empty result from sfparse_base64decode(). R CMD
   check rejects compiled code that can terminate R. Each site is marked
   "zuhttp: was abort()".
3. nghttp2_map_print_distance() in nghttp2_map.c, which writes to stderr and
   was guarded by !WIN32 alone, is compiled only under DEBUGBUILD, which
   stays undefined.
4. NGHTTP2_STATICLIB is defined, so NGHTTP2_EXTERN is empty and
   $(C_VISIBILITY) hides every nghttp2 symbol (D-66); BUILDING_NGHTTP2 is
   defined as upstream's own builds do.
5. nghttp2/nghttp2ver.h is generated from nghttp2ver.h.in by the script,
   which checks it against the copy in the release tarball.
6. HAVE_CONFIG_H is left undefined, which skips config.h; src/Makevars.in
   defines HAVE_ARPA_INET_H, HAVE_NETINET_IN_H, HAVE_CLOCK_GETTIME and
   HAVE_DECL_CLOCK_MONOTONIC=1, and src/Makevars.win.in HAVE_WINDOWS_H and
   HAVE_GETTICKCOUNT64.

The script compiles the patched tree and fails if any object references
abort, exit, printf, fprintf, vfprintf, puts, stderr, stdout, rand or an
assert handler.
